slug: radiculopathy-myelopathy-neuropathy
title: Root, Cord or Nerve? Localising a Neurological Lesion
area: Skills · Neuro Exam
level: Clinical
best: 3rd year onwards
minutes: 14
hook: Numb hands and weak legs can come from a root, the spinal cord or the peripheral nerves — and the treatments, and the urgency, are completely different. Learn the pattern that tells them apart. || Sunn haath aur kamzor taangein root, spinal cord ya peripheral nerves se aa sakti hain — aur ilaaj aur urgency bilkul mukhtalif hain. Woh pattern seekhein jo inhein alag karta hai.
goal: By the end, you'll tell radiculopathy, myelopathy and peripheral neuropathy apart using reflexes, tone, sensory pattern and weakness, and decide who needs urgent referral. || End tak aap reflexes, tone, sensory pattern aur kamzori se radiculopathy, myelopathy aur peripheral neuropathy ko alag karenge, aur tay karenge ke kise urgent refer karna hai.

say: Three questions locate the lesion: **(1) What do the reflexes and tone do?** Reduced = lower motor neuron (root, plexus or nerve); brisk and stiff = upper motor neuron (cord or brain). **(2) What is the shape of the sensory loss?** A strip (dermatome) = root; a patch matching a nerve = peripheral nerve; both feet and hands in a glove-and-stocking pattern = polyneuropathy; a level on the trunk with loss below = cord. **(3) Which muscles are weak?** A myotome = root; a nerve's muscles = nerve; both legs and trunk = cord. || Teen sawal lesion ki jagah batate hain: **(1) Reflexes aur tone kya karte hain?** Kam = lower motor neuron (root, plexus ya nerve); brisk aur sakht = upper motor neuron (cord ya dimagh). **(2) Sensory kami ki shakal kya hai?** Patti (dermatome) = root; nerve se milta patch = peripheral nerve; dono pair aur haath glove-and-stocking pattern mein = polyneuropathy; trunk par level aur neeche kami = cord. **(3) Kaun se muscles kamzor hain?** Myotome = root; nerve ke muscles = nerve; dono taangein aur trunk = cord.
analogy: Think of the nervous system as a motorway network. A **root** problem is one slip road closed (a narrow band is cut off). A **peripheral nerve** problem is one A-road cut (one named territory). A **polyneuropathy** is potholes at the far ends of every road (toes and fingertips first). A **cord** problem is the motorway itself blocked: everything below that point is affected and the traffic behind piles up (brisk reflexes). || Nervous system ko motorway network samjhein. **Root** ka masla ek slip road band hona hai (ek tang patti kat jati hai). **Peripheral nerve** ka masla ek A-road ka katna hai (ek naam wali territory). **Polyneuropathy** har sarak ke door sirey par gaddhay hain (pehle toes aur fingertips). **Cord** ka masla khud motorway ka block hona hai: us point ke neeche sab affect hota hai aur peechay ka traffic jam ho jata hai (brisk reflexes).
compare: Three patterns side by side || Teen patterns ek saath
head: Lesion || Lesion ;; Typical findings || Aam findings ;; Urgency || Urgency
row: Root (radiculopathy) || Root (radiculopathy) ;; Reflex reduced at that level; one myotome weak (wasting if chronic); a dermatomal strip of numbness, often with arm or leg pain; tone normal || Us level ka reflex kam; ek myotome kamzor (chronic mein wasting); dermatomal patti sunn, aksar arm ya leg ke dard ke saath; tone normal ;; Usually non-urgent unless the weakness is progressive || Aam taur par non-urgent jab tak kamzori progressive na ho
row: Cord (myelopathy) || Cord (myelopathy) ;; Brisk reflexes below the level, clonus, Babinski, Hoffmann; spasticity; clumsy hands and gait trouble; a sensory level and band-like trunk feeling || Level ke neeche brisk reflexes, clonus, Babinski, Hoffmann; spasticity; anari haath aur gait ki takleef; sensory level aur dhar par band jaisa ehsaas ;; Often urgent: the cord can be permanently damaged || Aksar urgent: cord ko hamesha ke liye nuksan ho sakta hai
row: Peripheral nerve or polyneuropathy || Peripheral nerve ya polyneuropathy ;; Reduced or absent reflexes (ankles first in polyneuropathy); one nerve's muscles, or distal symmetrical weakness; nerve territory or glove-and-stocking numbness || Kam ya gayab reflexes (polyneuropathy mein pehle ankles); ek nerve ke muscles, ya distal symmetrical kamzori; nerve territory ya glove-and-stocking numbness ;; Depends on the cause; rapid progression is urgent || Wajah par depend; tez barhna urgent
check: A 60-year-old has clumsy hands, difficulty with buttons, a stiff walk, brisk knee jerks and a positive Hoffmann sign. Where is the lesion? || 60 saal ke patient ke haath anari hain, button lagana mushkil, sakht chaal, brisk knee jerks aur positive Hoffmann sign. Lesion kahan hai?
ok: The cervical spinal cord (degenerative cervical myelopathy) || Cervical spinal cord (degenerative cervical myelopathy) || Yes — clumsy hands, gait change and UMN signs point to the cord. This needs a medical review and imaging, not neck manipulation. || Haan — anari haath, gait mein tabdeeli aur UMN signs cord ki taraf ishara karte hain. Medical review aur imaging chahiye, gardan ki manipulation nahi.
no: A C6 nerve root || C6 nerve root || A root lesion gives reduced reflexes and a dermatomal pattern, not brisk reflexes and gait change. || Root lesion mein reflexes kam aur dermatomal pattern hota hai, brisk reflexes aur gait ki tabdeeli nahi.
no: Peripheral neuropathy || Peripheral neuropathy || Neuropathy gives reduced reflexes and glove-and-stocking sensory loss. || Neuropathy mein reflexes kam aur glove-and-stocking sensory kami hoti hai.
demo: dermatomes/c7 :: C7 dermatome :: A true C7 radiculopathy gives pain and numbness down the back of the arm into the **middle finger**, with weak elbow extension and a reduced triceps jerk. Watch the zone, then picture the three findings lining up: dermatome, myotome and reflex. || Sahi C7 radiculopathy arm ki peeth se **middle finger** tak dard aur numbness deti hai, elbow extension kamzor aur triceps jerk kam. Zone dekhein, phir tasawwur karein ke teeno findings milti hain: dermatome, myotome aur reflex.
steps: A quick localising routine || Jaldi localise karne ka routine
step: Ask about the story :: Pain that travels in a band, clumsy hands, gait change, bladder or bowel symptoms, symmetrical numb feet, a nerve-specific trigger (carpal tunnel at night). || Kahani poochein :: Band mein safar karta dard, anari haath, gait mein tabdeeli, bladder ya bowel symptoms, symmetrical sunn pair, nerve-specific trigger (raat ko carpal tunnel).
step: Look at tone, reflexes and plantar responses :: Brisk plus stiff points above the root; reduced points to the root or nerve. || Tone, reflexes aur plantar responses dekhein :: Brisk aur sakht root se upar ki taraf; kam root ya nerve ki taraf.
step: Map the sensory loss on a body chart :: Strip, nerve patch or glove-and-stocking, with a clear upper border or not. || Sensory kami ko body chart par map karein :: Patti, nerve patch ya glove-and-stocking, upar ka saaf kinara ho ya nahi.
step: Test myotomes and compare with nerves :: Find a muscle that shares the root but not the nerve (and the reverse). || Myotomes test karein aur nerves se compare karein :: Aisa muscle dhoondein jo root share kare magar nerve nahi (aur ulta).
step: Decide urgency and act :: Cord signs, progressive weakness or sphincter change need same-day medical review; stable root or nerve problems can be managed and monitored. || Urgency tay karein aur action lein :: Cord signs, barhti kamzori ya sphincter tabdeeli ka usi din medical review; stable root ya nerve masle manage aur monitor ho sakte hain.
mistake: **Anchoring on the neck or back.** A stiff, painful neck does not mean the neck is the problem: carpal tunnel, ulnar neuropathy and cord compression all mimic "cervical radiculopathy". Another trap is trusting a single test. Spurling's test is specific but not sensitive; a negative test does not exclude a root problem, and a normal reflex does not exclude cord disease early on. Always combine findings. || **Gardan ya kamar par atak jana.** Sakht, dardnak gardan ka matlab yeh nahi ke masla gardan mein hai: carpal tunnel, ulnar neuropathy aur cord compression sab “cervical radiculopathy” ki naqal karte hain. Ek aur jaal: ek test par bharosa. Spurling test specific hai lekin sensitive nahi; negative test root ke masle ko rule out nahi karta, aur normal reflex shuruat mein cord ki bimari ko rule out nahi karta. Hamesha findings ko mila kar dekhein.
case: Mr A, 52, builder: three months of neck pain with burning down the right arm into the thumb and index finger, worse looking up. || Reduced right biceps and brachioradialis jerks, weak elbow flexion and wrist extension (grade 4/5), reduced pinprick over the thumb and index finger, no UMN signs, Spurling positive. Pattern: C6 radiculopathy (an C5–C6 disc). || Neck positioning and traction trial, nerve-gliding exercises, scapular and deep neck flexor strengthening, ergonomics; avoid end-range loaded neck extension; review in 2 weeks with referral if power drops. || At 4 weeks arm pain is 3/10 (from 7/10), biceps jerk back to 1+, power 5/5; sensation normal. Continue the programme and plan return to full duties.
clinic: **Write the localisation down.** "Right C6 radiculopathy: reduced biceps and brachioradialis jerks, 4/5 elbow flexion and wrist extension, reduced pinprick thumb and index, no UMN signs." One line like that tells the doctor, the next therapist and you which system you examined and what you found. If you cannot place the lesion, say so and refer: "pattern unclear, mixed UMN and LMN signs." || **Localisation likh dein.** “Right C6 radiculopathy: biceps aur brachioradialis jerks kam, elbow flexion aur wrist extension 4/5, thumb aur index par pinprick kam, UMN signs nahi.” Aisi ek line doctor, agle therapist aur aap ko batati hai ke aap ne kaun sa system dekha aur kya paya. Agar lesion ki jagah na bata sakein to saaf likhein aur refer karein: “pattern wazeh nahi, mixed UMN aur LMN signs.”
check: Which finding is the strongest reason to **refer urgently** in a patient with neck pain and arm symptoms? || Gardan ke dard aur arm ke symptoms wale patient mein urgent refer karne ki sab se mazboot wajah kaun si hai?
ok: New clumsy hands, a gait change, brisk reflexes and bladder urgency || Naye anari haath, gait mein tabdeeli, brisk reflexes aur bladder urgency || Yes — together these suggest progressive cord compression, which can cause permanent damage if not treated quickly. || Haan — yeh milkar progressive cord compression batate hain, jis se agar jaldi ilaaj na ho to hamesha ka nuksan ho sakta hai.
no: Pain that is worse in the morning || Subah zyada hone wala dard || Morning stiffness alone is not a cord sign. || Sirf subah ki sakhti cord sign nahi.
no: Numbness in one dermatome that is slowly improving || Ek dermatome ki numbness jo aahista behtar ho rahi hai || An improving single-root deficit is reassuring. || Behtar hota hua single-root deficit tasalli bakhsh hai.
reveal: Why do reflexes become *reduced* at the level of a cord lesion but *brisk* below it? || Cord lesion ke level par reflexes *kam* aur uske neeche *brisk* kyun hotay hain? || At the damaged level, the reflex arc itself (root or anterior horn cells) is hurt, so that reflex is lost (lower motor neuron sign). Below it, the arc is intact but has lost its inhibition from the brain, so it overreacts (upper motor neuron sign). The pair marks the level: **inverted supinator** at C5–C6 is the classic example. || Kharab level par reflex arc khud (root ya anterior horn cells) zakhmi hoti hai, is liye woh reflex jata rehta hai (lower motor neuron sign). Uske neeche arc theek hai lekin dimagh se inhibition kho chuki hai, is liye over-react karti hai (upper motor neuron sign). Yeh jora level batata hai: C5–C6 par **inverted supinator** classic misaal hai.
evidence: For **degenerative cervical myelopathy**, no single test is reliable; a cluster of gait deviation, positive Hoffmann, inverted supinator sign, Babinski and age above 45 greatly raises the probability, and the average delay to diagnosis is still more than two years. For **lumbar radiculopathy**, the straight-leg raise is sensitive but not specific, and the crossed straight-leg raise is specific but not sensitive; two or more positive findings together are best. || **Degenerative cervical myelopathy** ke liye koi ek test bharosay ka nahi; gait deviation, positive Hoffmann, inverted supinator sign, Babinski aur 45 saal se zyada umar ka cluster probability ko bohat barhata hai, aur tashkhees mein ausat der ab bhi do saal se zyada hai. **Lumbar radiculopathy** ke liye straight-leg raise sensitive lekin specific nahi, aur crossed straight-leg raise specific lekin sensitive nahi; do ya zyada positive findings ka saath hona behtar hai.
check: Which combination best fits a **peripheral polyneuropathy**? || Kaun sa combination **peripheral polyneuropathy** se sab se behtar match karta hai?
ok: Symmetrical glove-and-stocking numbness with reduced ankle jerks || Symmetrical glove-and-stocking numbness aur kam ankle jerks || Yes — the longest nerves fail first, so toes, feet and fingertips and the ankle jerks go first. || Haan — sab se lambi nerves pehle fail hoti hain, is liye toes, pair, fingertips aur ankle jerks pehle jaate hain.
no: Band-like trunk sensation with brisk leg reflexes || Dhar par band jaisa ehsaas aur brisk leg reflexes || That points to the cord. || Yeh cord ki taraf ishara hai.
no: One myotome weak with matching dermatomal loss || Ek myotome kamzor aur usi dermatome mein kami || That points to a nerve root. || Yeh nerve root ki taraf ishara hai.
safety: **Refer the same day** for any of: new bladder or bowel dysfunction, saddle numbness, progressive or bilateral limb weakness, sensory level on the trunk, a new gait disturbance with UMN signs, or neurological signs after trauma or with fever, cancer history or unexplained weight loss. Do not manipulate the neck or back while these are unresolved. || **Usi din refer karein** agar in mein se koi ho: bladder ya bowel ki nayi kharabi, saddle numbness, barhti ya dono taraf ki kamzori, trunk par sensory level, UMN signs ke saath nayi gait kharabi, ya trauma ke baad, bukhar, cancer ki history ya be-wajah wazan ghatne ke saath neurological signs. Jab tak yeh hal na hon gardan ya kamar ko manipulate na karein.
summary: Ask three questions: what do reflexes and tone do, what shape is the sensory loss, which muscles are weak. || Teen sawal poochein: reflexes aur tone kya karte hain, sensory kami ki shakal kya hai, kaun se muscles kamzor hain.
summary: Root = reduced reflex, one dermatome and myotome; cord = brisk reflexes, clumsy hands, gait change; nerve = nerve territory or glove-and-stocking with reduced reflexes. || Root = kam reflex, ek dermatome aur myotome; cord = brisk reflexes, anari haath, gait mein tabdeeli; nerve = nerve territory ya glove-and-stocking aur kam reflexes.
summary: Combine findings, never trust one test, and refer the same day for cord signs, sphincter change, saddle numbness or progressive weakness. || Findings ko mila kar dekhein, ek test par bharosa na karein, aur cord signs, sphincter tabdeeli, saddle numbness ya barhti kamzori par usi din refer karein.
card: Three questions to localise a neurological lesion? || Neurological lesion localise karne ke teen sawal? || Reflexes and tone (UMN or LMN)? Shape of the sensory loss? Which muscles are weak? || Reflexes aur tone (UMN ya LMN)? Sensory kami ki shakal? Kaun se muscles kamzor?
card: What finding pattern suggests cervical myelopathy? || Kaun sa finding pattern cervical myelopathy batata hai? || Clumsy hands, gait change, brisk reflexes, Hoffmann or Babinski, age over 45. || Anari haath, gait mein tabdeeli, brisk reflexes, Hoffmann ya Babinski, 45 saal se zyada umar.
card: Why do ankle jerks go first in polyneuropathy? || Polyneuropathy mein ankle jerks pehle kyun jaate hain? || The longest nerves fail first (length-dependent), so the most distal reflexes and sensation go earliest. || Sab se lambi nerves pehle fail hoti hain (length-dependent), is liye sab se distal reflexes aur sensation pehle jaate hain.
card: What is an inverted supinator sign? || Inverted supinator sign kya hai? || Tapping brachioradialis gives finger flexion but no elbow flexion: a C5–C6 cord lesion (arc damaged at C6, release below). || Brachioradialis tap karne par finger flexion lekin elbow flexion nahi: C5–C6 cord lesion (C6 par arc kharab, neeche release).
deeper: UMN vs LMN lesson || /learn/umn-vs-lmn || The compare-and-contrast that underpins every localisation. || Har localisation ki buniyad wala compare-and-contrast.
deeper: Red flags screening lesson || /learn/red-flags-screening || When neurological signs mean urgent referral. || Neurological signs kab urgent referral matlab hain.
source: Davies BM, et al. Degenerative cervical myelopathy. BMJ. 2018;360:k186. || degenerative cervical myelopathy BMJ review
source: Rubinstein SM, Pool JJM, van Tulder MW, et al. A systematic review of the diagnostic accuracy of provocative tests of the neck for diagnosing cervical radiculopathy. Eur Spine J. 2007;16:307–319. || diagnostic accuracy provocative tests of the neck cervical radiculopathy
